    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green. The full test suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (which handles `POST /api/owners`).\n\n**Change:** When a create request carries an `Idempotency-Key` header whose value was already seen on a previous successful create, the endpoint now returns the originally created owner with **200 OK** instead of creating a duplicate (which would otherwise hit the duplicate-identity/household checks and 409).\n\nDetails in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n- Added an in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer> idempotentCreates` mapping each seen key to the created owner's id.\n- At the top of `addOwner`, if the request's `Idempotency-Key` is already recorded, it fetches that owner and returns it with 200.\n- After a successful create/save, it records `key \u2192 owner.getId()`.\n- Since the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi` method signature is fixed, the header is read from the current request via `RequestContextHolder` (a small `currentIdempotencyKey()` helper that returns the non-blank header value, or `null`).\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreIdempotentRepeat` (first POST \u2192 2xx, repeat with same key \u2192 200, same id) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS` confirms the whole suite is green.",
