    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners` (`addOwner`), from the request arriving to the response.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. The caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else the method is never entered.\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, triggering a 400 on failure). Constraints from `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern .*\\S.*`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern .*\\S.*`\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max 10)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern .*\\S.*`\n   - `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern .*\\S.*`\n   - `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 In the method body (each in this exact order)\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit.** Read the non-blank `Idempotency-Key` header. If it was seen on a prior successful create and that owner still exists, return the original owner with **200 OK** \u2014 no further validation, no new side-effects.\n4. **Email validate + normalize** (`normalizeEmail`, mutates the DTO). Blank \u2192 set to `null`. Otherwise trim + lowercase; if it fails `EMAIL_PATTERN` \u2192 **400**; if its domain is in the disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400**; else the lowercased value is stored back on the DTO.\n5. **Postcode validate + normalize** (`normalizePostcode`, mutates the DTO). Blank \u2192 `null`. Must be exactly 4 digits; when the city maps to a known region (`OwnerMapper.CITY_REGION`), the postcode must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); otherwise \u2192 **400**.\n6. **Address validate + normalize** (`normalizeAddresses`, mutates the DTO). Prefers a non-blank `addressLine1` (normalizes line1/line2, composes them into `address`, clears line2 if absent); otherwise normalizes the flat `address` and clears the structured lines. Normalization = trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`/`RD\u2192ROAD`/`AVE\u2192AVENUE`. If no address is supplied in either form \u2192 **400**.\n7. **City-capacity check** (`countOwnersInCity`). If the city (case-insensitive) already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n8. **Telephone normalize to E.164** (`toE164`, mutates the DTO). Strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps an explicit `+`country code or assumes `+61` (dropping one leading `0`); requires 8\u201315 digits and, for a known code, the exact national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). On failure \u2192 **400**; else the normalized telephone is set on the DTO.\n9. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` candidate** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n10. **Identity (contact) duplicate check.** Compute `identityContact` = `<telephone>|<email>`. If any non-deleted existing owner has the same contact identity \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n11. **Household duplicate check.** Compute `householdId` (SHA-256 of normalized last name + postcode). If a non-deleted owner already shares that household and the request does **not** set `sharesHousehold=true` \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**. If it does share and `sharesHousehold` is true, the owner is marked a *declared member* (`declaredMember=true`).\n12. **Registration-date resolution + future check.** If no `registrationDate` supplied, default to today; else if it is after today \u2192 **400** (no future registration). Then roll forward to the next business day (`toBusinessDay`, skipping weekends and the fixed 2026 holidays).\n13. **Daily sign-up limit** (`countOwnersRegisteredOn`). If \u2265 100 owners already registered on that adjusted business day \u2192 **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Side-effects on the owner (all validations passed)\n\n14. Set `registrationDate` to the adjusted business day.\n15. Set `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` \u2014 region derived from postcode (fallback city, then `UNKNOWN`) + first 8 upper-hex chars of SHA-256(telephone + lastName); de-duplicated by appending `-<n>` on collision.\n16. Set `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive), measured before this insert.\n17. Set `bulkSignupWarning` = `true` if > 80 owners already registered on that business day.\n18. Set `householdSize` = existing household members + 1.\n19. Set `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` \u2014 for a declared member, forced to `false`/`null`; otherwise flags a soft match (same last name + postcode, different telephone; lowest-id match wins).\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Persistence and post-write side-effects\n\n20. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (assigns the id).\n21. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and the mapper-derived `membershipLevel` / `membershipNumber`.\n22. **Record idempotency key** \u2014 store `key \u2192 owner.id` in `idempotentCreates` (only if a key was present).\n23. **Build response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **201 CREATED**.\n\nNote that a number of the returned `OwnerDto` fields (e.g. `salutation`, `initials`, `ageBand`, `membershipPoints/Level`, `checkDigit`, `timezone`, `identityKey`, `fiscalYear`) are computed on the fly by `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` at step 23 \u2014 they are derived in the response, not stored side-effects."
